# Playwright e2e

- Discovery: `tests/helpers/fetchAppLinks.ts` crawls the rendered [App Builder](https://shapediver.github.io/GrasshopperExampleModels/11-AppBuilder/definitions.html) and [BETA](https://shapediver.github.io/GrasshopperExampleModels/BETA/definitions.html) pages. Do not parse `definitions.md` — those files are stubs filled from `examples.json` at docs build. Every discovered slug gets smoke + visual tests; `scenarioActions.ts` only adds interactions.
- Scenarios: `tests/config/scenarioActions.ts` — one entry per slug: `params` (e.g. `g` for settings file), `actions(page, slug)` or `namedActions[]` (one Playwright test per name). E-commerce and tools APIs have dedicated specs (`tests/specs/ecommerceApi.spec.ts`, `tests/specs/toolsApi.spec.ts`) so they do not duplicate smoke/visual of `example-executeActions`. Those specs loop a named `actions[]` (one Playwright test per API method).
- Helpers: `viewportCoords` (normalised to the canvas bounding box; canvas starts at **x=300** in the default layout), `waitForModelRecomputed`, `takeSnapshot`, `getParameterElement`, `getStandardContainer` / `setViewportBelowMobileBreakpoint` / `setViewportBelowNavbarBreakpoint` / `openAppShellNavbar` / `expectAppShellNavbarCollapsed` (`tests/helpers/appBuilderContainers.ts`; AppShell `md` is 992px; collapsed navbar uses the `hidden` attribute — Playwright `toBeHidden()` is not reliable because Mantine CSS keeps a layout box). E-commerce and tools e2e both use the localhost parent on `http://127.0.0.1:3000` (`tests/fixtures/cross-window`, iframe `name="app"`). E-commerce: `openCrossWindowScenario`, parent `__connector`. Tools: `openToolsApiScenario` (`?api=tools`), Open agent stubbed to `window.parent` because deployed App Builder sends COOP `same-origin` (a popup to localhost has `window.opener === null`); parent `__toolsApi`. SDV, recompute, and notifications use `sdvTarget(page)` (the iframe). Settings `agentOverride` is a test intercept so Open agent appears; App Builder source is unchanged. `example-ecommerceApi` covers every connector method except `addToCart` (dummy parent rejects after creating a model state). `example-toolsApi` covers every in-scope generic tool. `example-mobileFallback` (`public/example-mobileFallback.json`) covers AppShell theme + JSON overlay + one-hop chain: desktop slots, closed-navbar portrait/landscape layout (leftover `right` in the grid), and open-navbar drawer contents. `example-mobileFallback-grid` (`public/example-mobileFallback-grid.json`) is the same remapping on Grid (no burger; leftover `left` / `right` / `bottom` all on screen). `example-mobileFallback-tabs` covers a tabbed source container and extras landing in a tabbed target’s active tab. `example-mobileFallback-anchors` covers 3d default-to-right vs JSON overlay, 2d theme isolation, and closed-anchor `previewIcon` swap. `example-mobileFallback-keepBottom` covers AppShell `keepBottomInGrid` leftover bottom in the main grid.
- Device: Desktop Chrome. `use.viewport` is 1280x800 but the project's `devices["Desktop Chrome"]` sets 1280×720, which is what snapshots capture. Hardware GL via `launchOptions.args` (`--use-angle=d3d11` on Windows only, `--ignore-gpu-blocklist --enable-gpu` everywhere), needed for the gizmo drags of the interaction examples. Mobile-fallback cases resize below `md` (390×844 portrait, 900×700 landscape).
- Deterministic snapshots: `public/example-simple-interaction-colors.json` via `params: {g: ...}` instead of pixel tolerances. Rectangle/gumball `automaticSceneUpdate` examples use the same solid interaction colors.
- New behaviours get a scenario entry; models not yet on the test server get the **entry without running it**.
- Interaction examples (SS-10024), `public/example-<rectangle|gumball|drawing>-<basic|alwaysActive|alwaysActive-automaticSceneUpdate>.json` plus `example-gumball-alwaysActive-automaticSceneUpdate-resetValue.json` (`settings.resetValue: ""`, the gizmo restarts after each update):
    - Scenarios: `tests/config/interactionExampleScenarios.ts` (one simple and one complex `namedActions` entry per file; sent values are parsed from the PUT body with `transformValueFromBody`, `collectPageErrors` catches page errors). Shared locators, waits and gestures live in `tests/helpers/interactionExamples.ts`; every gesture asserts that it moved the object (`boundsChanged`), because Confirm is enabled as soon as a box is selected and a missed drag would otherwise pass. The former deep scenarios (camera orbit, a move while a request is in flight, ...) timed out on CI runners and were removed.
    - Multi-parameter examples (bug reports of SS-10024): `example-rectangle-multi-automaticSceneUpdate.json` (testing-account `ss-10024-one-parameter-per-box-2`: three always active, automatically updating rectangle transforms, one box each, in the left container) and `example-rectangle-anchors-automaticSceneUpdate.json` (`ss-10024-floating-containers-2`: the same parameters each in a 2D anchor opened by a `selecton` action slot and closed by `selectoff`; anchors are exclusive, so selecting another box closes the open one). The anchors example loads the model's own App Builder output (3000 ms timeout). The multi example overrides it with a copy of the model's App Builder data whose `automaticSceneUpdateTimeout` is 30000: the second move must start before the countdown ends, and on CI runners a mouse step takes about 0.6 s, so the click on the second box (which restarts the countdown, the pointer hold pauses it only while pressed) was followed by the drag 5 s later and the update rebuilt the gizmo mid-drag (CI run 40678471752). `moveTwoBoxesQuickly` computes all screen points up front and runs both quick drags back to back (`dragMouse(..., quick)`). Asserted: one request carries both boxes (`expectBoxesSent`, parameters `RectangleTransform1` = `box_translated`, `RectangleTransform2` = `box_original`), no request right after the second move (the restart of the countdown is covered by the scheduler's unit tests), a later move resends the other parameter's value, a move whose anchor closes meanwhile is still sent, and empty containers are not shown: the left container (toolbar parameters plus text widgets without text) is hidden; in the anchors example it appears once the text widgets show the sent values (`containerElement(page, "left")` outside the viewport, then inside), in the multi example it stays hidden because the override keeps the text widgets static, the anchor of a selected box opens with a hidden panel because its parameter renders in the toolbar (`anchorPanel(page, id)` has count 1 and is hidden).
    - `automaticSceneUpdate` is alwaysActive-only (gumball, rectangle transform, drawing). The basic files carry `automaticSceneUpdate: true` too and the basic tests wait past the idle timeout before Confirm to prove it is ignored. The examples set `automaticSceneUpdateTimeout: 3000` (default 500) so that the pending state is observable on slow runners; `IDLE_WAIT` is 5000. The automaticSceneUpdate files also set `buttons.clear: false` (drawing: `general.buttons.clear`), so those tools offer no control at all (`expectDrawingDirty("automatic")` asserts the absence of Confirm, Cancel and Clear). The basic and alwaysActive rectangle and gumball tests end with Clear (`clearAndExpectReset`: the request carries no transformation, the box is back at its initial bounds). The transform examples reference their parameter from a `controls` widget only (in the alwaysActive files the parameter renders in the toolbar, so the left container renders nothing and is laid out like an absent one: `containerElement(page, "left")` is not in the viewport, see `.cursor/rules/empty-containers.mdc`).
    - Rectangle/gumball files were generated from the App Builder output of testing-account `rectangletransform-6-2-3` (loaded once, copied, settings adjusted; 3 boxes `box_original` / `box_transformed` (tilted) / `box_translated`; rectangle `maximumSelection: 1`, gumball 3). That model's `RectangleTransform` is a **custom App Builder Interaction parameter** in the GH JSON (`parameters[]`), not a session parameter; `appBuilderOverride` replaces GH JSON, so the custom parameter is re-declared with `settings.type` and the `controls` widget refs use `sessionId: "default_appbuilder"`. Gumball overrides `type: "gumball"` and drops the rectangle-only props (`corners`, `midpoints`, `plane`, `rotation`, `scaling`).
    - Drawing uses `2i-pointsinputsimpleexample` (`Boundary`) with accordion `overrides` (deep-merged into GH `settings` by `applyOverrides`): basic sets `general.presentation: "widget"`, alwaysActive sets `"toolbar"` (or the GH widget wins). A single alwaysActive drawing toggle is read-only and is **not** promoted to a toolbar checkbox (`resolveRuntimeToolbarGroups`); assert the **Drawing settings** menu instead.
    - Positions come from the scene at runtime (`tests/helpers/sceneCoords.ts`: `camera.project` of node bounding boxes / parameter values), never from fixed canvas coords: the camera re-frames after the first customization and the geometry moves with every transform. Click boxes at the projected bounding-box center (the top face center of the tilted box lies outside it). The gumball handle is center + 48 px and needs a hover update before the press (`dragMouse` approaches from an offset; a quick press grabs the pivot).
    - Values are **absolute placements**: a request carries the current placement of every transformed box (including the model's own transform of `box_transformed`); a fresh gizmo on a transformed box re-emits that placement, so Confirm without a move may resend an unchanged matrix. Customizations are counted as PUT requests to `/output` (`trackCustomizations`). Gumball/rectangle must **not** PUT on select (identity gizmos); after an idle PUT the gizmo is recreated on the new nodes.
    - Rectangle translation (dragging the base plane through the object) needs the Viewer changes of SS-10024 (published since `@shapediver/viewer.*` 3.22.0-next.42, which `package.json` requires; older Viewers deselect the object instead). The plane is only grabbed away from the scaling handles, so `planeTranslate` zooms in first (`zoomInOnNode`); the other gestures use corner scaling and the rotation handle. A press near a scaling handle without movement rescales (the point jumps to the pointer).
    - `rectangletransform-6-2-3` and `2i-pointsinputsimpleexample` must be in `modelstorage.slugs.ts`; `pnpm run convert-slug-data` refreshes the hourly platform access token in `modelstorage.local.ts` (an expired token shows "Invalid token" / 403 on localhost) and skips slugs whose model no longer exists.

## Deploy / global setup

Global setup caches the app links (public pages plus the testing account, which needs `PLATFORM_CLIENT_ID` and the platform access key/secret from `.env.platform-access`), runs `pnpm i` (skipped with `APPBUILDER_E2E_SKIP_INSTALL=1` or in CI) and deploys the HEAD of the checkout the tests run from to `TEST_BRANCH` (default `testing/local`) via `pnpm run publish` (needs a clean tree per `git status --porcelain`, so untracked example files block it until committed; tsc 0, sentry-cli, AWS credentials, `.env`). `SKIP_DEPLOY=1` skips the deploy, CI skips it unless `APPBUILDER_E2E_DEPLOY=1`, and a tag already pointing at HEAD skips it as well. A stale local `testing/local` branch **blocks** the deploy.

**Do not deploy or rerun e2e unless the user asks.**
